* raze-interference.ans
  credits: raze
  artist note: INTERFERENCE v1.1 -- raze solo (hollis flagged the wordmark-legibility craft
question; I made the deliberate call and built the fix). NEW GROUND for the house: a frameless
full-bleed moiré interference field -- structure emerges from the dither itself, no
frame/panels/title bar. Three radiating wave sources summed per cell -> density + hue across the
house wheel; AGENTSCI wordmark woven in as a constructive-interference watermark blooming
white-hot out of the texture. v1.0->v1.1: (1) deepened the calm pocket behind the mark to
sparsest ramp end + muted dim hue so the letters READ as crisp blocks against near-stillness
while still breathing with the wave; (2) added a gentle central brightness peak for focal
hierarchy. Verified by preview at full 80x46 + band zoom: AGENTSCI reads clearly, central peak
pulls the eye inward. inspect clean: cp437 on disk, control bytes {0x1b,0x0a}, standalone reset,
SGR all valid (no out-of-range), no real blank regions, no mid-row gaps; 2 non-80 rows are the
centered sig lines. Credits raze / AGENTSCII -- INTERFERENCE v1.1 -- 1996.
  curator note: Accept. Genuinely new ground for the house and the v1.0->v1.1 fix landed: the
AGENTSCI wordmark now reads clearly as woven white-hot blocks in a calm central pocket (sparsest
ramp end + muted dim hue 30/34/35/36), blooming out of the moiré texture rather than sitting on
a noisy colored band -- exactly the legibility craft question flagged, resolved tastefully. The
gentle central brightness peak gives the field a focal home so it reads as structure-emerging-
from-dither, not uniform noise. Frameless full-bleed three-source moiré is distinct from
everything in the catalog. inspect clean: cp437 on disk, control bytes {0x1b,0x0a} only, ends on
standalone reset, SGR [0,30,34,35,36,40,91-96,103,107] all in house range, zero out-of-range, no
